1
1. BATTERY 63.18 kWh NOMINAL, 56.86 kWh USABLE AT 90 % DEPTH OF DISCHARGE. 9 No. FOXESS CQ7 LFP MODULES IN SERIES AT
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
14980.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   518.4 V NOMINAL, ONE MASTER AND 8 SLAVES, ON BATTERY PORT 1 OF THE THREE THE INVERTER PROVIDES.
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
14360.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
2. POWER IS SET BY THE PORT, NOT BY THE CELLS. 80 A AT 518.4 V IS 41.5 kW CONTINUOUS, WHICH IS 0.66 C ON THIS STACK,
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
13740.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   AND 110 A FOR 60 SECONDS IS 57.0 kW. THE INVERTER WOULD TAKE 240 A ACROSS ALL THREE PORTS.
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
13120.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
3. THE SITE LOAD IS 3.3 TIMES THE PV GENERATION, SO THERE IS ALMOST NO SURPLUS TO STORE. A BATTERY CHARGED ONLY
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
12500.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   FROM PV SURPLUS WOULD CYCLE ABOUT TWELVE TIMES A YEAR AND WOULD NOT BE WORTH FITTING. IT EARNS ITS PLACE BY
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
11880.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   BEING CHARGED OFF PEAK AND BY CARRYING THE OUTAGE, WHICH IS WHY THE CONTROL ABOVE IS BUILT THE WAY IT IS.
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
11260.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
4. THE ANNUAL GRID PEAK IS NOT REDUCED. IT FALLS ON A DECEMBER AFTERNOON WHEN THERE IS NO PV LEFT AND THE STATE
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
10640.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   OF CHARGE IS PINNED AT THE FLOOR THAT PROTECTS THE 18:00 OUTAGE. HOURS SPENT OVER THE TARGET DO FALL, BY
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
10020.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   35.5 %. LOWERING THE ANNUAL MAXIMUM AS WELL WOULD NEED A SECOND CQ7 STACK ON PORT 2, OR AN AGREEMENT TO
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
9400.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   ACCEPT A SHORTER BACKUP THROUGH THE WINTER. THAT IS A COMMERCIAL DECISION, NOT AN ELECTRICAL ONE.
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
8780.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
5. 223.9 EQUIVALENT FULL CYCLES A YEAR. AT A TYPICAL LFP WARRANTY OF 6000 CYCLES TO 70 % THAT IS WELL BEYOND THE
0
TEXT
8
07-TEXT
10
3000.0
20
8160.0
30
0.0
40
225.0
1
   TWENTY FIVE YEAR LIFE OF THE ARRAY, SO CAPACITY FADE RATHER THAN CYCLE COUNT WILL DECIDE WHEN IT IS REPLACED.
0
